*.md
.cache

# NEVER let a real credential enter the build context. The Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .`, so without this every `.env*` on the build host lands in a
# BUILDER-STAGE layer: `PB_ADMIN_PASS`, `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `SESSION_SECRET`,
# `ADMIN_SECRET`, `CONSUELA_ENCRYPTION_KEY` and `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` among them.
# The runtime image is slim (`COPY --from=builder` pulls only .next/public/
# node_modules/package.json/deploy.sh/docker-compose.yml/docs), so these were
# never in the shipped container — but builder layers persist on the NAS, and
# the deploy dir is synced with tar, which never deletes, so a stale copy
# outlives the local file it came from.
#
# `.env.example` stays: it is the committed, placeholder-only contract.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.docker
.env.local
.env.integration
.env.production

# AppleDouble sidecars from past macOS `tar` syncs. Inert for the build (TS
# include-globs skip dot-prefixed files) but they are 5,382 files of noise and
# they are not part of the repo.
._*

